@startuml d-02-token-topology
' D-02 — the three token topologies between Transmit, PingFederate and DCP.
' PROPOSAL generated by AI from SRC-ADR (DCP consumes PingFederate tokens; a token exchange is
' required). Option A is drawn to record that it was refused, not overlooked.
title D-02 — who exchanges the CIAM token for the token DCP accepts

participant "Bank app /\nlogin screen" as ui
participant "Transmit CIAM" as ciam
participant "PingFederate" as ping
participant "ASPSP gateway" as gw
participant "Core adapter" as core
participant "DCP" as dcp

group Option A — the gateway calls DCP with the Transmit token (refused)
  ciam -> gw : Transmit token
  gw -> dcp : call with a Transmit token
  dcp --> gw : refused
  note right of dcp #FFDDDD
    Contradicts SRC-ADR: DCP services
    require a PingFederate token.
  end note
end

group Option B — exchange at PingFederate, called by the core adapter (recommended)
  ciam -> gw : Transmit token
  gw -> core : read or submit
  core -> ping : RFC 8693 exchange over mTLS (V1, Q-04)
  ping --> core : PingFederate token (cached for the session, V3)
  core -> dcp : call with a PingFederate token
  dcp --> core : answer
end

group Option C — CIAM federates to PingFederate, one token from the start (check first)
  ui -> ciam : PSU authenticates
  ciam -> ping : federation (V2)
  ping --> gw : PingFederate token
  gw -> core : read or submit
  core -> dcp : call with the token it already has
  dcp --> core : answer
end

note over gw
  Whichever option: the gateway should trust exactly
  one issuer for the authority it acts on. Who signs
  the assertion that SCA happened is Q-16 (A-17).
end note
@enduml
